<title>SOUTH KOREA: Trigem says buying back 100,000 shrs.</title>
<headline>Trigem says buying back 100,000 shrs.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Trigem Computer Inc said on Tuesday it would buy back 100,000 shares of its own stock in the open market between January 11 and April 10 to boost its stock price.  </p>
<p>The buyback, representing 1.11 percent of its share capital, will be made by Dongsuh Securities, Daishin Securities and Kyobo Securities, Trigem said in a statement.</p>
<p>Trigem holds 1.18 percent of its common shares, it said.</p>
<p>The statement said buy orders would be placed at the previous day's closing price.</p>
<p>Trigem shares closed at 21,000 won on Tuesday, down 1,400.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
